# The admin portal now ships: /admin is served live and talks to the serverless
# API in api/, which stores posts and images by committing them to the repo.
#
# server.js stays out. It is the local-only equivalent of api/, and leaving a
# server.js in the project root makes Vercel detect this as a Node server app
# ("No entrypoint found") instead of a static site.
#
# Leading slashes anchor these to the project root. Without them, a bare
# "tools/" also matches assets/img/tools/ and strips the training-page logos.
/server.js
/tools/

# Secret — never ship this.
data/admin-password.txt

# data/posts.json and assets/img/uploads/ ARE deployed on purpose: the blog page
# reads posts.json as a static file when there is no live API.
